  "helpFaqTitle": "Common questions",
  "helpLoginQuestion": "Why can’t I sign in?",
  "helpLoginAnswer": "Sign-in needs an internet connection. Check your connection and try again. If Google sign-in fails, restart it or use email and password if your account has a password. Use Forgot password to reset an existing password.",
  "helpVehicleQuestion": "How do I set up or switch vehicles?",
  "helpVehicleAnswer": "Open My Garage from the vehicle selector on Garage. Add your vehicle there, or select another vehicle to see its records. Your plan determines how many vehicles you can add.",
  "helpDriverVehicleAnswer": "Your organization assigns your vehicles. Use the vehicle selector to switch between assignments. If no vehicle appears, contact your fleet administrator. Vehicle details and maintenance plans are managed by your organization.",
  "helpMaintenanceQuestion": "How do I record maintenance?",
  "helpMaintenanceAnswer": "Choose the correct vehicle, then open Maintenance to view its plan and history. Register a completed service with its date, odometer, and cost. Recording planned work updates the linked plan item. Drivers can log services, while their organization manages the plan.",
  "helpExpensesQuestion": "Where do I track costs and fuel?",
  "helpExpensesAnswer": "Expenses shows costs for the selected vehicle. Add an expense with its category, date, and amount. Use Refuel or Charge to record fuel quantity or charging energy. Check existing records before entering the same cost again.",
  "helpSyncQuestion": "What happens when I am offline?",
  "helpSyncAnswer": "After signing in, core records can be used offline. Changes wait on this device until they sync. Reconnect and check Sync status; use the manual sync action if needed. Do not uninstall or clear app data while changes are waiting. Sign-in, account changes, and some online features still need a connection.",
  "helpNotesQuestion": "Are my Notes backed up?",
  "helpNotesAnswer": "Notes are private to your account on this device. They do not sync or have a server backup. Uninstalling AutoX or clearing app data can remove them. Keep a separate copy of important notes before changing devices.",
